# AMD64 thunk export spec -- pdh.dll.
#
# WHY THIS MODULE, AND WHY IT LOOKED LIKE HEAP CORRUPTION.  DOOM (2016) ends
# its startup with
#
#     FATAL ERROR: Memory corruption before block!
#
# and that message is a misdiagnosis by the game, not a report of damaged
# memory.  Measured, on a frozen process: every live allocation's tail canary
# was intact under GlobalFlag=0x10 -- ~19,600 of them swept every two seconds
# for a whole run, zero damaged -- every subheap chain walked cleanly, and all
# 13,578 of the game's own blocks still validated against their own cookie,
# right up to the instant the message was printed.  Nothing had been written
# past the end of anything.
#
# What the check actually ran on was a pointer id Tech's allocator never
# returned.  Patching DOOM's FatalError entry with `jmp rdi` in the live
# process -- rdi is callee-saved and the free path sets it to rcx-0x10 -- made
# the emulator print the guest register file at the failure:
#
#     RCX=14200D380 ("Memory corruption before block!")
#     RDI=3FEF6D18ADC0  RSI=3FEF6D18ADD0
#     R10=0x66 ('f')  R9=0x736C ("ls")  R8=0x8075000500200008
#
# The "tag" is the letter 'f', the "offset" is the letters "ls", and the
# "size" is `08 00 20 00 05 00 75 80` little-endian -- Wine's OWN struct block:
# block_size 8 (128 bytes), tail_size 32, base_offset 5, type 'u', flags LFH.
# So rsi pointed at a Wine allocation's data, the sixteen bytes DOOM read as
# its header were the tail of the neighbouring string ("...false >") plus that
# block header, and the whole thing is a free through the wrong allocator.
#
# The guest stack named the caller: DOOMx64vk.exe+0x19f4d40 allocates 0x58 = 88
# bytes with operator new, calls LoadLibraryW(L"Pdh.dll"), and binds five
# entry points -- PdhOpenQueryW, PdhCloseQuery, PdhAddCounterW,
# PdhGetFormattedCounterValue, PdhCollectQueryData -- the Performance Data
# Helper it reads CPU counters through.  When the load fails it takes a
# cleanup path that releases that object through the ENGINE's allocator
# (Mem_Free, which expects a sixteen-byte id Tech header) rather than through
# the operator delete that matches operator new.  That mismatch is latent on
# Windows because the load never fails there.  Here it did: this tree builds
# dlls/pdh as a native ppc64 module and generated no AMD64 thunk for it, so
# the guest loader had nothing to resolve and LoadLibraryW answered NULL.
#
# So the fix is the same one-line fix avrt, dbghelp and iphlpapi needed, and
# it is not per-title: any guest that probes for an optional Wine builtin gets
# NULL where Windows gives it a module, and what it does on that path is its
# own business.  Nothing here is hand-written -- the export list comes from
# this module's own .spec.
DLL pdh.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# pdh.h is not in the global probe (nothing else needs it), so it is appended
# here exactly as dbghelp appends dbghelp.h and iphlpapi appends iphlpapi.h.
# Without it every eligible export is refused as "no declaration in any Wine
# header" and the module emitted is a real PE with NO exports -- which loads,
# and would leave the five GetProcAddress calls answering NULL, i.e. the same
# cleanup path and the same fatal error one step further along.
PROBE-EXTRA   pdh.h
